{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1440666-v5-in-dark-ages-any-attempts","id":1440666,"title":"V5 in Dark Ages: Any Attempts?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-03-19T18:06:45-07:00","id":1440666,"title":"V5 in Dark Ages: Any Attempts?","content":"Hi.<br /> Im thinking about starting a chronicle of V5 set in the dark ages, but I wanted to know if any of you have tried that and, of course, any personal experiences or feedback. I'm not really interested in the lore, or the presence of elders, but the actual mechanics (handling touchstones, humanity, combat, resonances, etc).<br /> <br /> Can you tell me anything about it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5394-argonot","name":"Argonot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-20T01:27:05-07:00","id":1440693,"title":"","content":"Armour is literally useless for vampires in v5, how am I going to accomplish my dreams of playing a vampire knight, huh?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-20T01:28:47-07:00","id":1440694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1440666-v5-in-dark-ages-any-attempts?p=1440693#post1440693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Armour is literally useless for vampires in v5, how am I going to accomplish my dreams of playing a vampire knight, huh?</div> </div> </div> </div>Was armor useful in dark ages?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-20T01:35:39-07:00","id":1440695,"title":"","content":"Less than reality, but enough to be worthwhile mechanically, especially DAV20's updated rules. up to 6 dice of protection I believe. In V5 it might... help you intimidate people? That's all it's good for if you're a vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-20T02:08:27-07:00","id":1440698,"title":"","content":"The V20DA Disciplines are the best versions so far (including V5). I'd just use that ruleset. <br /> <br /> You could port over the V5 Humanity system, but DA has a much bigger role for Roads, so you'll lose a lot of that flavour by doing so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-20T02:54:17-07:00","id":1440701,"title":"","content":"I was thinking about treating armor like extra health levels, perhaps? Light armor one, medium two, heavy three? Something like that...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5394-argonot","name":"Argonot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-20T03:48:58-07:00","id":1440704,"title":"","content":"<br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Argonot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1440666-v5-in-dark-ages-any-attempts?p=1440701#post1440701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was thinking about treating armor like extra health levels, perhaps? Light armor one, medium two, heavy three? Something like that...</div> </div> </div> </div>From a storytelling/realism perspective, that doesn't really capture how useful armour is.<br /> From a gameplay perspective, that's a bit weird, because so many attacks ignore armour.<br /> <br /> The closest thing I'd say to getting armour to work in V5 with the system you've described is to have armour add to the difficulty to hit. IE you need two successes to hit someone in light armour, three for heavy armour, four for.... but then that's too strong. Perhaps you could have armour reduce the damage done? Perhaps, since rolls are generally Attribute+Skill+weapon VS Attribute+skill+weapon you could also add armour to each person's roll, as armour would also give you an offensive advantage realistically (Not needing to block a strike because you know the armour will take it, so you just attack while your opponent has left themselves open) </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1440666-v5-in-dark-ages-any-attempts?p=1440698#post1440698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The V20DA Disciplines are the best versions so far (including V5). I'd just use that ruleset.<br /> <br /> You could port over the V5 Humanity system, but DA has a much bigger role for Roads, so you'll lose a lot of that flavour by doing so.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oi if we just went for -this edition did things better- then nobody'd use anything recognizable as V5.<br /> <br /> As for DAV20 having the best disciplines, i simply must protest; Yes, celerity actually works now and presence actually has somewhat more concrete rules behind it, but you've also got some of the most -what-the-fuck-were-they-thinking- changes pre-2018. Level 1 Quietus, for example, is turning people's hearts into jars of blood so they can be diablerized later; what kind of lunatic thinks that's what the Assamite clan needs as a level 1 power?I could cite so many other problems, but I don't wanna derail the thread (too much)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 03-20-2021, 06:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-20T16:09:59-07:00","id":1440768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1440666-v5-in-dark-ages-any-attempts?p=1440704#post1440704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> Perhaps, since rolls are generally Attribute+Skill+weapon VS Attribute+skill+weapon you could also add armour to each person's roll, as armour would also give you an offensive advantage realistically (Not needing to block a strike because you know the armour will take it, so you just attack while your opponent has left themselves open) </span></span></span><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This sounds fantastic. Thanks for the idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5394-argonot","name":"Argonot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-21T02:34:28-07:00","id":1440817,"title":"","content":"Armor in the High Middle Ages was extremely effective, so, yeah, if you want to keep things in line with history, armor needs to be effective.<br /> <br /> Shields were also very effective. And bucklers were carried by many a civilian.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance Writer and Storyteller's Vault contributor. Find my work here: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/index.php?affiliate_id=17903\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.storytellersvault.com/ind...liate_id=17903</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1535-jackob","name":"Jackob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1535_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-21T08:35:20-07:00","id":1440831,"title":"","content":"I have seen multiple people on different Discords and Reddit talk about their V5 Dark Ages. Common changes often include things like changing some skills like Drive and Technology, using Humanity and having Convictions be picked from the various Roads sins, and Bane changes mainly.<br /> <br /> Here is one from a Discord I'm part of: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/11PV33trTNp-32hdZ7-XSdW3ooh2uPlBA/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/11PV...ew?usp=sharing</a><br /> <br /> So something to remember about this as well, is that V5's combat is meant to be cinematic, not realistic. So 'because it did a thing in real life' isn't generally a concern; same reason why there aren't eleventy-billion different weapon statistics, adds and other stuff.<br /> <br /> From a mathematical, making armor d things like reduce damage or add difficulty to hit will make a moderately-competent combatant nigh invincible, especially when combined with Fortitude's physical powers. Which is kind of really against the point of V5's combat, writ large, when the ideal is to be done in three or so turns. It will turn combat into a crazy slog. Which is fine if you want that kind of slog, but is at the very least not within the existing design space.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1808,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","user":"elmerg","date":". 03-21-2021, 11:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-22T03:36:00-07:00","id":1440925,"title":"","content":"I use this for morality in DAV5:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.v5homebrew.com/wiki/Long_Hard_Road_Out_of_Hell\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.v5homebrew.com/mw/resources/assets/poweredby_mediawiki_88x31.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.v5homebrew.com/wiki/Long_Hard_Road_Out_of_Hell\" target=\"_blank\"> Long Hard Road Out of Hell - V5 Homebrew Wiki </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.v5homebrew.com/wiki/Long_Hard_Road_Out_of_Hell\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.v5homebrew.com/wiki/Long_Hard_Road_Out_of_Hell </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I also use a ruleset for combat and armor, but is written in spanish, I think it would be easy to translate with goolge, so I'm posting it here just in case:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/117LJjprTmKzyuA7MVp4ZZJw8MVrMdYzCkJ-zyg83sfM/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/117LJjprTmKzyuA7MVp4ZZJw8MVrMdYzCkJ-zyg83sfM/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/117LJjprTmKzyuA7MVp4ZZJw8MVrMdYzCkJ-zyg83sfM/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/117LJjprTmKzyuA7MVp4ZZJw8MVrMdYzCkJ-zyg83sfM/edit?usp=sharing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25915-nicolai","name":"nicolai","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-22T07:16:06-07:00","id":1440942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nicolai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1440666-v5-in-dark-ages-any-attempts?p=1440925#post1440925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I use this for morality in DAV5:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.v5homebrew.com/wiki/Long_Hard_Road_Out_of_Hell\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.v5homebrew.com/mw/resources/assets/poweredby_mediawiki_88x31.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.v5homebrew.com/wiki/Long_Hard_Road_Out_of_Hell\" target=\"_blank\"> Long Hard Road Out of Hell - V5 Homebrew Wiki </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.v5homebrew.com/wiki/Long_Hard_Road_Out_of_Hell\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.v5homebrew.com/wiki/Long_Hard_Road_Out_of_Hell </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I also use a ruleset for combat and armor, but is written in spanish, I think it would be easy to translate with goolge, so I'm posting it here just in case:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/117LJjprTmKzyuA7MVp4ZZJw8MVrMdYzCkJ-zyg83sfM/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/117LJjprTmKzyuA7MVp4ZZJw8MVrMdYzCkJ-zyg83sfM/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/117LJjprTmKzyuA7MVp4ZZJw8MVrMdYzCkJ-zyg83sfM/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/117LJjprTmKzyuA7MVp4ZZJw8MVrMdYzCkJ-zyg83sfM/edit?usp=sharing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>These help, certainly. Long Road Out of Hell is something I started reading a few days ago and like quite a bit. Though, you still lose something. <br /> <br /> I would also change the benefits of each Humanity level (e.g., Blush of Health, Eat Food) to provide more specific Merits according to the Road chosen. Tzimisce on Metamorphosis don't need Blush of Health or food, because they're interested in other things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-23T11:03:10-07:00","id":1441094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nicolai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1440666-v5-in-dark-ages-any-attempts?p=1440925#post1440925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I use this for morality in DAV5:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.v5homebrew.com/wiki/Long_Hard_Road_Out_of_Hell\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.v5homebrew.com/mw/resources/assets/poweredby_mediawiki_88x31.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.v5homebrew.com/wiki/Long_Hard_Road_Out_of_Hell\" target=\"_blank\"> Long Hard Road Out of Hell - V5 Homebrew Wiki </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.v5homebrew.com/wiki/Long_Hard_Road_Out_of_Hell\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.v5homebrew.com/wiki/Long_Hard_Road_Out_of_Hell </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I also use a ruleset for combat and armor, but is written in spanish, I think it would be easy to translate with goolge, so I'm posting it here just in case:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/117LJjprTmKzyuA7MVp4ZZJw8MVrMdYzCkJ-zyg83sfM/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/117LJjprTmKzyuA7MVp4ZZJw8MVrMdYzCkJ-zyg83sfM/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/117LJjprTmKzyuA7MVp4ZZJw8MVrMdYzCkJ-zyg83sfM/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/117LJjprTmKzyuA7MVp4ZZJw8MVrMdYzCkJ-zyg83sfM/edit?usp=sharing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>Native spanish speaker here. Your contribution will be much appreciated. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5394-argonot","name":"Argonot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-25T08:57:25-07:00","id":1441379,"title":"","content":"I actually did my take on it a while ago on my podcast:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://wodarkages.squarespace.com/podcast/5-suggestion-for-a-new-edition\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"http://static1.squarespace.com/static/5f352e879e84e0597aeaee4d/t/60155135c1c9ac6a1fb21e46/1612009783315/Side+Quests+small.jpg?format=1500w\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://wodarkages.squarespace.com/podcast/5-suggestion-for-a-new-edition\" target=\"_blank\"> 5 Suggestion for a new edition </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://wodarkages.squarespace.com/podcast/5-suggestion-for-a-new-edition\" target=\"_blank\"> https://wodarkages.squarespace.com/podcast/5-suggestion-for-a-new-edition </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> In this Side Quests, Jacob presents his 5 ideas for a new edition of Dark Ages Vampire. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance Writer and Storyteller's Vault contributor. Find my work here: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/index.php?affiliate_id=17903\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.storytellersvault.com/ind...liate_id=17903</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1535-jackob","name":"Jackob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1535_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-25T11:47:12-07:00","id":1441402,"title":"","content":"There is 1 episode of la by night. Sort of a flashback episode set during what I assume is the French revolution.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/19506-killtron","name":"Killtron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar19506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-31T18:17:02-07:00","id":1442217,"title":"","content":"I'm running Giovanni Chronicles in V5, and the only adjustments I made were: calling Streetwise Hearth Wisdom, and Firearms just Shooting (slings, bow, crossbow...), Technology is until the Industrial Revolution an empty Skill, and for a person to know how to read in the Languages she knows would need Academics 2 (I made a Merit for literation but my Players didn't like it). And of course, Drive is tied to riding and driving wagons. <br /> Most Advantages are still pretty much what they were, with Resources just taking a less liquidated form. I've made also 10 to 15 Loresheets, about the matters of the social classes (the pariahs, the commoners, the merchants, the warriors, the nobles, the clerics...) and faiths, with some extra thrown in (like knowing how to travel and contraband, being related to the crusades, having access to monasteries...etc). <br /> <br /> I haven't used or thought much of armors, but I suppose we either keep it the way it is, make it mitigate Superficial/Aggravated damage (which might be OP), or be more complex and have armors have both an Aggrav. to Superficial dmg rating, and a Superficial dmg Absorb rating, but that seems a bit too much for me.<br /> <br /> With the amount of travel and info dispersal in Medieval Times, I'm also a bit more lax with the intervals between interactions with Touchstones (I got a mechanic that kind of needs the PC to visit, send a letter, know through someone else, or something, that his/her Touchstone is ok; generally a week), but this is a kind of homebrew so it isn't worth going into.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-01T05:30:57-07:00","id":1442243,"title":"","content":"<i>Dark Eras 2</i> in CofD proposes &quot;touchstone mementos&quot;, which are objects that remind the character of their touchstones, a bit like fetters without the mysticism.<br /> I don't see the need to make armour useful for vampires. Wear it if you want to pass for a mortal soldier and not get caught surviving grievous injuries, otherwise enjoy being supernaturally resilient.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-01T08:26:17-07:00","id":1442255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1440666-v5-in-dark-ages-any-attempts?p=1442243#post1442243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see the need to make armour useful for vampires. Wear it if you want to pass for a mortal soldier and not get caught surviving grievous injuries, otherwise enjoy being supernaturally resilient.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but mortals might want to wear it... and some vampires will probably want to armor up their ghoul bodyguard. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance Writer and Storyteller's Vault contributor. Find my work here: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/index.php?affiliate_id=17903\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.storytellersvault.com/ind...liate_id=17903</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1535-jackob","name":"Jackob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1535_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}